abstract: >-
  Open-source, human-in-the-loop framework that closes the loop between local
  microstructure and macroscopic magnetic properties. A Random Forest trained on
  sparse annotations segments SEM-EDS data, phase identities follow from
  stoichiometric rules held in external JSON files, and an Isolation-Forest
  anomaly map flags unclassified regions. An independent module extracts Curie
  temperatures from M(T) curves by automated dual-tangent intersection. The two
  modules run standalone or merge into one correlative database linking phase
  fractions, chemistry and magnetic transitions.
keywords:
  - materials characterisation
  - scanning electron microscopy
  - energy-dispersive X-ray spectroscopy
  - image segmentation
  - random forest
  - Curie temperature
  - permanent magnets
  - human-in-the-loop
